A kernel 2.6.39 doesn't boot on my POWER MAC G4.  A kernel 2.6.38.6 with
almost the same config boots without any problems. I see messages about
initialization *99_core and 3 white lines. The system doesn't boot 
father. There
isn't any messages in logs about this boot. I guess it is a first step 
in initialization
of kernel. A kernel 2.6.38-rc3 has the same problem.

